Z||000000||Boomtastic||11-04-2001||02:19 PM||||I just returned from a trip to Canada and spotted an interesting Fiero just outside Calais Maine on Route 9. It was lime green with oversize rear tires on it. It also had a big "bug grabber" type scoop facing rear-ward. I couldn't stop the 30' camper I was driving (running behind schedule) to take a picture or I would have. Anyone know anything about this vehicle? Any pics? I wish I could have stopped. I'm willing to place bets it had an eight in it ..<P>Btw, this was Fiero #2 I had seen on the trip. It amazes me that I can drive 1100 miles and only see 2 Fieros. Heck - I can do that without leaving the house.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Boomtastic<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mirror_md_clr.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||jelly2m8||11-04-2001||09:30 PM||||Was this a fast back? If so I seen this car about 5 years ago at night as we were passing through there. Didn't have the chance to check it out.<P> If this is the same car, it's cool that buddy still has it.<P>BTW I just came back from FL, and after a 2300 mile drive from FL to NS, I didn't see 1 single Fiero, except the one sitting on the flat deck behind me the whole way home....<P> I'll post more on my trip on my tread. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Boomtastic||11-04-2001||09:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jelly2m8:<BR><B>Was this a fast back? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Nope- it was a notchback, approx. 1984 - 86 vintage, although at the speeds I was puching the camper I could be mistaken on the year.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||1
